<title>BRAZIL: Brazil bank plans another $420 mln in bonds in '97.</title>
<headline>Brazil bank plans another $420 mln in bonds in '97.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's national development bank, BNDES, plans to tap an additional $420 million from international capital markets this year.</p>
<p>A BNDES spokeswoman, who requested anonymity, said the bank would probably raise the money through two international bond issues. She said bank officials had not decided which markets they would tap.</p>
<p>&quot;We have plans to borrow a total of $1 billion in 1997. We already did a $295 million Italian lira deal and we raised $285 million from loans,&quot; she added.</p>
<p>((--John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414))</p>
